PROPOSAL ONLY. Not applied. Repo stays read-only on branch fyd-factory.

Patch 01: stamp data-object-anchor on tenant site sections (src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx)

Rationale: MarginObjectLayer anchors objects to document elements via
[data-object-anchor="<key>"]. Tenant site sections currently carry no
anchor keys (only src/app/page.tsx does), so the layer has nothing to
track on tenant sites. This patch stamps the deterministic section id
(pageSlug:component:index, already the section id contract) onto a
thin wrapper. No visual change intended; the wrapper is an unstyled
block div, and sections already render as block-level.

Verified seams: SitePageView at renderer.tsx:1795 maps
page.sections via renderSection(s, ctx, i) (lines 1795-1801 read on
2026-09-23). Section id determinism: FYDSection.id = pageSlug +
":" + component + ":" + index (sitespec/types.ts).

Caveat: the wrapper div can disturb margin-collapsing in section CSS.
Acceptance requires before/after screenshots of both demo tenants
(happy-place, coppersmith-plumbing) at desktop and mobile widths.

--- a/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
+++ b/src/fyd/components/renderer.tsx
@@ -1795,7 +1795,11 @@ export function renderSection(section: FYDSection, ctx: RenderContext, motionInd
 export function SitePageView({ page, ctx }: { page: FYDPage; ctx: RenderContext }) {
   return (
     <>
       <FydMotionStyles theme={ctx.spec.themeTokens} />
-      {page.sections.map((s, i) => renderSection(s, ctx, i))}
+      {page.sections.map((s, i) => (
+        <div key={s.id} data-object-anchor={s.id}>
+          {renderSection(s, ctx, i)}
+        </div>
+      ))}
     </>
   );
 }
